{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 149,
    "dDurationMs": 4911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Happy 500,000!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5060,
    "dDurationMs": 6590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you guys so much for subscribing to\nmy channel and for joining me on this scientific"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11650,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adventure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12650,
    "dDurationMs": 3399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, if you got 500,000 people together\nand we all held hands in a line, it would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16049,
    "dDurationMs": 7761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stretch from Sydney to Melbourne or from San\nFrancisco to San Diego or from London to Inverness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23810,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Oy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24810,
    "dDurationMs": 2639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What are you forming a line here for?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27449,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are going to scare off Nessy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29669,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30669,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I suppose I should get down to answering\nyour question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32470,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go ahead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33470,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hit me with your best shot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34470,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I understand that the sky is blue do to\nRayleigh scattering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38060,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Short wave lengths get scattered way more\nand blue light dominates because it is so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42780,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "short."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43780,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that is the case, why isn’t the sky violet?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46020,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Ok, here is the thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47820,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sky isn't really blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is bluish white."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52440,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the sky is illuminated by the sun and the\nsun in its all colors, but not equally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57920,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun doesn’t emit that much red, nor\ndoes it emit that much violet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61850,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of the light it emits is kind of in the\ngreeny part of the spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64860,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now as you point out, due to Rayleigh scattering\nmore of the shorter wavelengths arte scattered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70080,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is why the sky looks blue, because\nit is basically the sun’s white spectrum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74610,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shifted a little bit towards the blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78040,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the spectrum of the blue sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79670,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, as you can see, it is quite broad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81210,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, in fact, there is a fair amount of violet\nlight in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84500,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is not as much violet light as there\nis blue light, because the sunlight that we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88570,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started with had much more blue than it has\nviolet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91780,
    "dDurationMs": 5210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e If I have a lap top on the international\nspace station with a hard disk drive in it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96990,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will the torque from its spinning cause the\nlap top to spin as well?\u003e\u003e"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101510,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, by the law of conservation of angular\nmomentum, yes, the lap top should spin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105979,
    "dDurationMs": 4661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I did a quick back of the envelope calculation\nand I found that if you spun up your hard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110640,
    "dDurationMs": 6830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disk from rest up to 5400 rpm, then it would\ncause the laptop to spin in the opposite direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117470,
    "dDurationMs": 5399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at a rate hat would cause it to do about one\nrevolution every 17 seconds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122869,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e What would happen if you poured liquid\noxygen on a fire?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126930,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Kaboom?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128720,
    "dDurationMs": 5029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Say you were able to pass the event horizon\na black hole and come back, what would coming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133749,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back look like of the person and for an observer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136769,
    "dDurationMs": 4731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Well, to an outside observer it would look\nas though you never came back at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141500,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to the person it would look as though\nyou didn’t come back either, because once"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145950,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are passed the event horizon, that is\nit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148279,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your entire future lies within the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151779,
    "dDurationMs": 4251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it will only be a matter of seconds before\nyou are in the singularity, the very core"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156030,
    "dDurationMs": 3389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this black hole and you are no longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159419,
    "dDurationMs": 5490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you could bring a rocket back with\nyou and try to fight it, if you tried to accelerate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164909,
    "dDurationMs": 6101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from the black hole, you would find that\nyou actually live for less time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171010,
    "dDurationMs": 6259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might see more space, but your time would\npass more slowly and so you would end up in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177269,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the singularity sooner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179750,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I guess the lesson is don’t fight it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183970,
    "dDurationMs": 3409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to live longer, just relax and\ngo with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187379,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e You have met a lot of interesting people\non your adventures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190749,
    "dDurationMs": 3051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is there someone specific that you would\nlove to meet?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193800,
    "dDurationMs": 5939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I would love to meet Bill Nye, Neil DeGrasse\nTyson, Richard Dawkins and President Obama"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199739,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a non scientist inclusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201540,
    "dDurationMs": 1199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I really like his book."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202739,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you haven’t read The Audacity of Hope\nthat is a good recommendation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206469,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e If all the galaxies are constantly accelerating\naway from each other, will they ever reach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210969,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light or stop accelerating all\ntogether?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213869,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e So, yeah, all the galaxies do seem to be\naccelerating away from each other, faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218379,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and faster, which makes this kind of a unique\ntime in the history of the earth, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222999,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right now we can still see that there are\nhundreds of billions of galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227799,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But sometime in the future due to the expansion\nof the universe, those galaxies will be so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232709,
    "dDurationMs": 6161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "far away and, yes, they will be receding at\nfaster than light speed and then you might"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238870,
    "dDurationMs": 2189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say: Well, nothing can go faster than light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241059,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it is kind of true in that these galaxies\nwon’t be moving through space at a speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245510,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster than light, but the space in between\nus and them will be expanding at a rate which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251120,
    "dDurationMs": 5609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means they will be moving relative to us faster\nthan light, if that makes any sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256729,
    "dDurationMs": 4081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So their light that they are emitting will\nnever be able to reach us, because it will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260810,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never be able to make progress through this\nexpanding space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263780,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is kind of interesting to think about what\nwill happen as that time approaches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268530,
    "dDurationMs": 4919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the light that is coming from those\ndistant galaxies travels across this expanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273449,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274449,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it becomes red shifted, cosmologically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277009,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And eventually the wave length of this light\nwill be so big that its wavelength is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281479,
    "dDurationMs": 3741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "size of the whole universe and that is impossible\nto detect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285220,
    "dDurationMs": 5550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at some point, probably about two trillion\nyears in the future we will only see our local"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290770,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cluster of galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292590,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the reason they haven’t gone out to\ninfinity, or very, very far away is because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296789,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are gravitationally bounded to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299090,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even though space is expanding on a large\nscale, the gravitational force is enough to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303300,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hold all of us together so we will be in it\nfor the long haul."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307110,
    "dDurationMs": 2899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this still means that there is going to\nbe strange cosmology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310009,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we are still around trillions of years\nfrom now, if we tried to look out, we would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313919,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see a very different universe, a universe\nwhich is much emptier than the one we see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317639,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318639,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we live at a unique point in space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321479,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We should appreciate that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322509,
    "dDurationMs": 3041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Is there such a thing as randomness in\nthe universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325550,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if so, isn’t that contradictory to science?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328260,
    "dDurationMs": 4909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Yes, I think there is randomness in the\nuniverse and, no, I do not think this contradicts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333169,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334169,
    "dDurationMs": 3291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though, perhaps you are thinking along the\nlines of Albert Einstein when he said: God"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337460,
    "dDurationMs": 1139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does not play dice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338599,
    "dDurationMs": 5161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He wasn’t happen when in quantum mechanics\nit seemed as though some events have probabilistic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343760,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outcomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344760,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, he thought that there were some hidden\nvariables there and we just didn’t know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347951,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what was determining the outcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349560,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we thought it was probabilistic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351479,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But all experiments seem to show, up to this\npoint, anyway, that there are some things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355580,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are randomly determined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357930,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are probabilistic in their nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360160,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, you can get quantum, random number\ngenerators and even the FBI and CIA can’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366060,
    "dDurationMs": 1849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seem to find any pattern in those numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367909,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they really, truly do seem to be random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370919,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, yes, it seems from all the experimental\nevidence that randomness is a fundamental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375789,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part of our universe, albeit mostly on the\nquantum scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379659,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e What shape is the universe and could light\nfrom our sun go around the universe and come"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385699,
    "dDurationMs": 2331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back and hit the other side of earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388030,
    "dDurationMs": 5830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e The shape of the universe seems to be flat,\nwhich means there is no large scale curvature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393860,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395000,
    "dDurationMs": 6229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the supposed reason for this is inflation,\nthis idea that very, very shortly after the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401229,
    "dDurationMs": 4871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big bang the whole universe just started accelerating\nat an incredibly fast rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406100,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even if it was kind of wiggly or warped\nor curved around on itself before inflation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411810,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after inflation it basically would have been\nflattened out, just like blowing up a balloon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416129,
    "dDurationMs": 3351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that side is going to become, you know, more\nor less flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419480,
    "dDurationMs": 4159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So within the limits of our observational\ncapabilities to these days, we think that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423639,
    "dDurationMs": 1481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the universe is flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425120,
    "dDurationMs": 4479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you go out in one direction you probably\nshouldn’t return the way you came."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429599,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, no, the universe does not appear to be\nclosed and you would probably never see the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433410,
    "dDurationMs": 1870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light coming up behind you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435280,
    "dDurationMs": 5910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Hey, man, I have one fantastic topic for\nyou to make a video about, but I need your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441190,
    "dDurationMs": 1259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "response."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442449,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You want to do it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444169,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Otherwise I contact Vsauce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447039,
    "dDurationMs": 5821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Hey, Michael, you want this one or shall\nI take it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452860,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e No, no, no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453860,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go ahead, Derek, take it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455069,
    "dDurationMs": 9391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e So we are really reaching the atomic size,\nbut not in some exotic laboratory device."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464460,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In every device you have in your computer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467900,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e How many transistors are on a chip now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471250,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e About a billion."
    } ]
  } ]
}
